Pilot-scale membrane capacitive deionization for water reclamation: Commissioning, performance benchmarking, and long-term assessment
Tsai-Hsuan Chen , Yu-Hui Kao , Yu-Yi Shen , Chen-Shiuan Fan *, Chia-Hung Hou *
Graduate Institute of Environmental Engineering, National Taiwan University, No. 1, Sec. 4 Roosevelt Rd., Taipei 10617, Taiwan
HIGHLIGHTS GRAPHICAL ABSTRACT
• Decision framework was presented for development of MCDI-based reclamation process. • Trade-offs among MCDI performance aspects were assessed during benchmark procedure. • Operating protocols were recommended for implementing MCDI in DWTPs. • MCDI achieved over 80% ion removal efficiency with 77% water recovery. • Long-term system stability was maintained with periodic acid cleaning.
